content.text:
Then I’d make the intrinsic:

**Death is Currency** — every corpse is a spell resource. The Necromancer can consume a corpse to pay the full cost of any spell instead of spending mana.

That’s genuinely strong and changes the whole economy:

- fights create future spell fuel;
- the Necromancer wants to preserve and position corpses;
- difficult encounters become more valuable instead of merely more dangerous;
- mana remains useful when there are no corpses.

It also gives us a clean foundation for future corpse-binding without making the intrinsic itself a summon button.

