content.text:
Mostly, yes—but with deliberate undead-runtime differences.

The resurrected mob uses the same authored monster identity and canonical spawn parameters, so it retains:

- the same monster type and abilities;
- authored stats, resistances, attacks, spells, and equipment;
- the same identity for content logic.

The differences are:

- faction becomes `summoned`;
- it is owned by the Necromancer;
- it gets a temporary lifespan based on monster power;
- it is marked `Reanimated`, so death produces bones instead of another corpse;
- its display name becomes `Risen <Monster Name>`.

It recreates the monster from its authored definition; it does not preserve the individual’s prior HP, statuses, or runtime history.

